Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• grid.address.city : city name we have to match (“Qianjiang”)  
• grid.id     : key we will join to publications.research_orgs  
• publications.research_orgs : ARRAY of GRID‑IDs that link a publication to an organisation / city  
• publications.date_inserted : filter – only rows whose year ≥ 2021  
• publications.journal.title : first‑priority venue title  
• publications.proceedings_title.preferred : 2nd‑priority venue title  
• publications.book_title.preferred : 3rd‑priority venue title  
• publications.book_series_title.preferred : 4th‑priority venue title  
Typical conditions  
• WHERE LOWER(grid.address.city) = 'qianjiang'  
• WHERE DATE(pub.date_inserted) >= '2021‑01‑01'  
• Join condition: grid.id = research_org_id (coming from UNNEST(pub.research_orgs))  

Below are ten exploratory BigQuery queries (all SELECT only, each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Look at all GRID records whose city is exactly ‘Qianjiang’.
SELECT id,
       name,
       address.city,
       address.country
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`
WHERE LOWER(address.city) = 'qianjiang'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Retrieve a few distinct city names that appear in the GRID table (sanity‑check).
SELECT DISTINCT address.city
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`
WHERE address.city IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Inspect the first 20 publications that contain at least one research_orgs entry.
SELECT id,
       ARRAY_LENGTH(research_orgs) AS org_cnt,
       research_orgs
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications`
WHERE ARRAY_LENGTH(research_orgs) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Check some publication rows inserted in 2021 or later.
SELECT id,
       date_inserted,
       journal.title AS journal_title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications`
WHERE DATE(date_inserted) >= '2021-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Join publications to GRID by any organisation located in Qianjiang (no date filter yet).
SELECT DISTINCT pub.id              AS publication_id,
                g.id                AS grid_id,
                g.address.city      AS city
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications` AS pub
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(pub.research_orgs) AS research_org_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`          AS g
  ON g.id = research_org_id
WHERE LOWER(g.address.city) = 'qianjiang'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Same as #5, but keep only publications inserted in 2021+.
SELECT DISTINCT pub.id AS publication_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications` AS pub
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(pub.research_orgs) AS research_org_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`          AS g
  ON g.id = research_org_id
WHERE LOWER(g.address.city) = 'qianjiang'
  AND DATE(pub.date_inserted) >= '2021-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Show every venue‑title component side‑by‑side for the filtered publications.
SELECT pub.id,
       pub.journal.title                       AS journal_title,
       pub.proceedings_title.preferred         AS proceedings_title,
       pub.book_title.preferred                AS book_title,
       pub.book_series_title.preferred         AS book_series_title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications` AS pub
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(pub.research_orgs) AS research_org_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`          AS g
  ON g.id = research_org_id
WHERE LOWER(g.address.city) = 'qianjiang'
  AND DATE(pub.date_inserted) >= '2021-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Build a single ‘venue_title’ field with the required priority logic.
SELECT DISTINCT
  COALESCE(pub.journal.title,
           pub.proceedings_title.preferred,
           pub.book_title.preferred,
           pub.book_series_title.preferred) AS venue_title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications` AS pub
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(pub.research_orgs) AS research_org_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`          AS g
  ON g.id = research_org_id
WHERE LOWER(g.address.city) = 'qianjiang'
  AND DATE(pub.date_inserted) >= '2021-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Return publication id together with the resolved venue title.
SELECT DISTINCT
  pub.id AS publication_id,
  COALESCE(pub.journal.title,
           pub.proceedings_title.preferred,
           pub.book_title.preferred,
           pub.book_series_title.preferred) AS venue_title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications` AS pub
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(pub.research_orgs) AS research_org_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`          AS g
  ON g.id = research_org_id
WHERE LOWER(g.address.city) = 'qianjiang'
  AND DATE(pub.date_inserted) >= '2021-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – distinct venue titles (deduplicated) meeting all requirements.
SELECT DISTINCT
  COALESCE(pub.journal.title,
           pub.proceedings_title.preferred,
           pub.book_title.preferred,
           pub.book_series_title.preferred) AS venue_title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.publications` AS pub
CROSS JOIN UNNEST(pub.research_orgs) AS research_org_id
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.dimensions_ai_covid19.grid`          AS g
  ON g.id = research_org_id
WHERE LOWER(g.address.city) = 'qianjiang'
  AND DATE(pub.date_inserted) >= '2021-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```
